      "description": "Item part of: National Film Board of Canada. Photothèque collection\nView of a tug boat hauling log booms up the coast from Stillwater to the log pond below the Powell River Company's mill.\nJuly 1944 / Powell River, B.C. — 1 item\nWRM REFERENCE NUMBERS:\n\nACCESSION:    1971-271\nREPRODUCTION:    e000762876 (copy negative number);\nCONSULTATION/REPRODUCTION:\n\nGraphics: photos\nRestrictions on access:  nil\nUSE/REPRODUCTION:\n\nRestrictions on use/reproduction:  nil\nCopyright:  Expired\nCredit:  Harry Rowed / National Film Board of Canada. Photothèque / Library and Archives Canada /\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION:\n26a\nnitrate neg. (Phototype)\n\"POWELL RIVER LOGGING AND PULP MILL OPERATIONS. Tough, snubbly little tugs bring the huge, quarter-mile-long booms up the coast from Stillwater to the log pond below the Powell River Company's mighty mill. Boom man here pole them to the jack ladder which carries them into the sawmill.\" (Inscription)\nWRM 5404 (Original item number)\nCREATORS: Rowed, Harry\n \n\nSOURCE: DAPDCAP 565972",
